```plaintext
0result.sql
```

0result.sql correctly:
• filters the crime records to the required period (2010‑2016) and the category “MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT”;  
• aggregates by year + month to get monthly counts;  
• applies MAX() per year to pick the single largest monthly value;  
• returns one row per year ordered chronologically.  

The other two SQL files (1result.sql and 2result.sql) are functionally identical, so any would work, but 0result.sql is the first, simplest, and already proven to yield the expected numbers shown in the CSV.